{"id": 10, "ts": 1780432997.9606128, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I concur with Sarah\u2019s assessment that Candidate\u202fC is the strongest overall fit. His ability to make correct decisions quickly, stay calm in a crisis, and understand complicated technology directly addresses decision quality, stress resilience, and technical competence\u2014key for long\u2011distance flights. Moreover, Sarah notes that he \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d which would satisfy crew cooperation and professional communication.\nHowever, my own notes flag two concerns: C has difficulty communicating ideas and is regarded as egocentric, and he is not very willing to further his education. These could affect ongoing learning and teamwork, especially on complex international routes.\nTo resolve this tension, could Emily share any observations on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s actual crew interaction and communication style during the interview? If his crew\u2011cooperation is indeed strong, I would maintain a vote for Candidate\u202fC; if not, we may need to reconsider."}
