{"id": 74, "ts": 1780433307.2266457, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I understand that the panel has been leaning toward Candidate\u202fC because of his rapid decision\u2011making and strong attention to detail. However, I\u2019m still convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the safer overall choice for a long\u2011distance pilot. B\u2019s very conscientious nature and proven ability to handle stress\u202fwell directly address operational reliability and stress resilience\u2014two non\u2011negotiable criteria for international flights. His skill in assessing weather conditions and excellent computer proficiency also demonstrate the technical competence we need for complex, long\u2011haul operations. While I acknowledge the concern that B can come across as pretentious and sometimes adopts the wrong tone, these communication issues are less severe than C\u2019s documented difficulty communicating ideas, his egocentric reputation, and his reluctance to pursue further education. Those latter traits raise serious doubts about crew cooperation, adaptability, and ongoing professional development. In my view, B\u2019s strengths in reliability, stress resilience, and technical ability outweigh his modest communication flaws, making him the stronger overall fit."}
